# Nothing here is required. The Mod SDK is found through Steam's own library
# list, mod projects through Mod HUB's settings, and the search index builds
# itself on first use. Set a variable only when detection gets it wrong.

# The Mod SDK install — the folder holding GameData and Editor.
# SE2_MODSDK=C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Space Engineers 2 - Mod SDK

# Where your own mod projects live, ';'-separated on Windows. A folder holding
# several projects expands to the projects inside it.
# SE2_MCP_MOD_ROOTS=C:\Users\<you>\Documents\SpaceEngineers2\Mods

# Where to keep the index and the field-documentation cache. Both are derived
# data, rebuildable at any time, and do not need backing up.
# SE2_MCP_CACHE=%LOCALAPPDATA%\se2-mcp

# --- Tool surface -----------------------------------------------------------
# 'core' exposes the 29 content tools (~7,000 tokens of schema) instead of all
# 60 (~12,200 tokens); 'mini' cuts to 13 (~3,400). Worth setting for a small
# local model.
# SE2_MCP_PROFILE=core

# Drop whole groups: knowledge, lookup, authoring, checking, logs, editor,
# modhub, blender.
# SE2_MCP_DISABLE=blender,editor

# Or name exactly the tools to expose, overriding both of the above.
# SE2_MCP_TOOLS=sdk_info,explain,mod_recipes,search_content,read_definition

# --- Bridges ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The in-editor plugin's HTTP port, and BlenderMCP's. Change only on a clash.
# SE2_MCP_BRIDGE_PORT=8765
# SE2_MCP_BLENDER_PORT=9876
